                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "2c17b3d0-5264-388b-a8d4-161a0f38947d",
                        "entry_id": "9f3f70d4-a312-31e8-8ec1-71f049345d00",
                        "glosses": [
                            "politische und wirtschaftliche Theorie, die die Abschaffung des Staates oder des Staatsmonopols zugunsten eines unregulierten freien Marktes, des Privateigentums, einer libertären Auslegung der persönlichen Freiheit und des Grundsatzes der Nicht-Aggression anstrebt"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "70b27a63-8781-413f-9325-5389d3fcdcde",
                                "sense_id": "2c17b3d0-5264-388b-a8d4-161a0f38947d",
                                "text": "Viele Menschen glauben, dass der Anarchokapitalismus in der Praxis nicht funktionieren kann."
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "ea06822f-8a39-4349-b192-1cd231cc3b9f",
                        "source_entry_id": "9f3f70d4-a312-31e8-8ec1-71f049345d00",
                        "source_sense_id": "2c17b3d0-5264-388b-a8d4-161a0f38947d",
                        "source_sense_description": "politische und wirtschaftliche Theorie für einen unregulierten freien Markt ohne staatlichen Einfluss",
                        "target_lang_word": "anarcho-capitalism",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "anarcho-capitalism",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b11fdeed-64af-3ef2-9ed9-dff4bd14e057",
                                        "entry_id": "04d2b64a-448b-380a-86e9-a3a700cf688b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A political and economic philosophy that advocates the elimination of the state and other coercive institutions in favour of individual self-ownership, voluntary society, and free market."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "839b5aba-fc6f-4404-bbb3-6249d09be284",
                                                "sense_id": "b11fdeed-64af-3ef2-9ed9-dff4bd14e057",
                                                "text": "Laissez-faire capitalism, or anarchocapitalism^([sic]), is simply the economic form of the libertarian ethic. Laissez-faire capitalism encompasses the notion that men should exchange goods and services, without regulation, solely on the basis of value for value. It recognizes charity and communal enterprises as voluntary versions of this same ethic."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ae43f139-dbfb-4199-afc4-b64e91de3b18",
                                                "sense_id": "b11fdeed-64af-3ef2-9ed9-dff4bd14e057",
                                                "text": "Anarcho-capitalism is a creed new to the present age. Its closest historical links are with the “individualist anarchism” of Benjamin R. Tucker and Lysander Spooner of the late nineteenth century, and it shares with Tucker and Spooner a devotion to private property, individualism, and competition. Furthermore, and in contrast to Read and Rand, it shares with Spooner and Tucker their hostility to government officials as a criminal band of robbers and murderers.[…]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "486a297c-dadf-3200-9dfb-4609303ef86f",
                                        "entry_id": "04d2b64a-448b-380a-86e9-a3a700cf688b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A political and socioeconomic system that ostensibly recognizes only individual self-ownership, voluntary society, and free market but not the state and other coercive institutions."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7cefc9a7-7fdf-462a-88f8-f553ebba1bc3",
                                                "sense_id": "486a297c-dadf-3200-9dfb-4609303ef86f",
                                                "text": "The second was shock therapy. Implemented briefly in the aftermath of the Soviet collapse, shock therapy aimed to construct a free market in post-communist Russia. It produced instead a species of mafia-dominated anarcho-capitalism."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "bf14fd00-ff91-4511-a40a-6f484fecb0e4",
                        "source_entry_id": "9f3f70d4-a312-31e8-8ec1-71f049345d00",
                        "source_sense_id": "2c17b3d0-5264-388b-a8d4-161a0f38947d",
                        "source_sense_description": "politische und wirtschaftliche Theorie für einen unregulierten freien Markt ohne staatlichen Einfluss",
                        "target_lang_word": "anarcho-capitalisme",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "anarcho-capitalisme",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0e657ab2-b6c9-3852-808c-0416dc050e54",
                                        "entry_id": "5af66595-3468-3e19-80e8-741725daa67c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Courant du libertarianisme prônant la suppression de l’État au profit d’un ordre fondé sur la propriété privée, l’échange et des institutions contractuelles ; revendiqué comme anarchiste par ses partisans et contesté par la plupart des traditions anarchistes."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Philosophie politique",
                                            "Économie politique"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "69fa9f38-c38f-454b-83e1-d1eaa6bd8c6a",
                                                "sense_id": "0e657ab2-b6c9-3852-808c-0416dc050e54",
                                                "text": "Murray Rothbard a fondé sa vision de l’anarcho-capitalisme sur la notion de droit de propriété."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6f1f98e1-b959-4d27-b3a2-10d3c1dafb6e",
                                                "sense_id": "0e657ab2-b6c9-3852-808c-0416dc050e54",
                                                "text": "Le terme de « minarchisme » est d’ailleurs plus correct que celui d’anarcho-capitalisme puisque, chez les libertariens, il n’y a pas grand-chose d’anarchiste à part une critique de l’État, au demeurant partielle et erronée."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
